;; The sim race (simrace.yml, clojure -M:simrace): runners that play the whole bot in the race's
;; captured worlds against the server model, on every core, from every landing with seed after
;; seed until the budget is spent. The real-server race (ci/race.edn) has the other runners.
{:simrace/runners 8                  ; GitHub runners, each a share of the worlds; the real race has eight, four stay free
 :simrace/sets ["R1" "R2" "R3" "R4"] ; the race's landing sets (ci/gym.edn), captured by simworld.yml
 :simrace/until "pearls-12"          ; the target each run plays every step up to: the Nether, the fortress (issue #261), seven blaze rods from its spawner (#262), in each set's captured Nether (#353) with the model's fortress spawners (#495), then twelve ender pearls from the model's warped-forest endermen (#263: they spawn, #523, and teleport and walk round walls, #542), as the real race (#516)
 :simrace/max-minutes 330            ; simulated minutes a run may take: the real bots' horizon, a lane's job (#252); a run that finishes early stops early
 :simrace/budget-minutes 330         ; wall minutes a runner plays: 300 took 303 with setup (sim race 38515210080), inside the job's 355 of GitHub's 360
 :simrace/heap-mb 11264}                ; the runner's 16 GB, less the system's share and the churn's 2 GB judge (issue #299)
;; A start at a fortress (issue #263/#262 frontier, branch ci/simrace-from-fortress): with
;; :simrace/from "fortress" each run starts in its set's captured Nether, on ground thirty-two
;; blocks (nearer when there is none) from the fortress spawner nearest the landing's Nether
;; coordinates, with the kit below, and plays only the stages from the blaze rods up to :simrace/until
;; (a failure before them is not the run's to file). Worlds whose Nether holds no spawner are left out.
;; Absent, every run starts from spawn in the overworld as before. --from fortress does the same on one
;; command line.
;;   :simrace/from "fortress"
;;   :simrace/kit {:stone_pickaxe 1 :cobblestone 256 ...}   ; replaces simrace/fortress-kit-default,
;;                                                         ; the real race's :race/kit
